    {
      "id": "claim_f6667b243e1b45f6aca3a4b821f11b65",
      "statement": "Service-layer classes (PaymentService, AuthorizationService, CaptureService, RefundService, VoidService, ConnectorMsgService, ClientService, ErrorService, ClientActivityService) follow a consistent pattern: they bind business parameters into ordinal-positioned input maps, register OracleTypes output parameters, call a named stored procedure via DBProcedureUtil, and translate the response_code into either a successful result map or an OracleException.",
